Feature: Telegram user authorization # features/authorization.feature:1
  As the bot owner
  I want only whitelisted Telegram users to interact with the bot
  So that unauthorized users cannot use the expense-report bot
  Feature: Telegram user authorization  # features/authorization.feature:1

  @story-11
  Scenario: Authorized user can send a free-text expense message                                                        # features/authorization.feature:12
    Given the bot is running                                                                                            # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the extraction service is working                                                                               # features/steps/common_steps.py:31
    And the database is empty                                                                                           # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given the bot authorization whitelist contains my Telegram user ID                                                  # features/steps/authorization_steps.py:26
    When I send a free-text expense message "coffee 3.50 eur at Central Cafe 2026-07-12" through the authorization gate # features/steps/authorization_steps.py:38
    Then the bot should send a reply                                                                                    # features/steps/authorization_steps.py:78

  @story-11
  Scenario: Unauthorized user is silently ignored and logged                                                            # features/authorization.feature:18
    Given the bot is running                                                                                            # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the extraction service is working                                                                               # features/steps/common_steps.py:31
    And the database is empty                                                                                           # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given the bot authorization whitelist does not contain my Telegram user ID                                          # features/steps/authorization_steps.py:32
    When I send a free-text expense message "coffee 3.50 eur at Central Cafe 2026-07-12" through the authorization gate # features/steps/authorization_steps.py:38
    Then the bot should not send any reply                                                                              # features/steps/authorization_steps.py:84
    And the unauthorized attempts log should contain my Telegram user ID                                                # features/steps/authorization_steps.py:90
    And the unauthorized attempts log should contain an ISO-8601 UTC timestamp                                          # features/steps/authorization_steps.py:96

Feature: CLI Expense Extraction and Storage # features/cli_extraction.feature:1
  As a developer
  I want to extract structured expense data from receipt images and free text via CLI
  So that I can verify the LLM extraction pipeline end-to-end without Telegram
  Feature: CLI Expense Extraction and Storage  # features/cli_extraction.feature:1

  @story-1
  Scenario: Extract expense from receipt image via CLI                  # features/cli_extraction.feature:11
    Given the LLM extraction service is available                       # features/steps/common_steps.py:23
    And the expense database is empty                                   # features/steps/common_steps.py:43
    Given a receipt image file "motorway_toll.jpg" with encoded content # features/steps/cli_steps.py:17
    When I run the CLI command "extract-from-image" with that image     # features/steps/cli_steps.py:24
    Then the extracted amount should be "3.80"                          # features/steps/common_steps.py:219
    And the extracted currency should be "EUR"                          # features/steps/common_steps.py:226
    And the extracted merchant should be "Autostrade per l'Italia"      # features/steps/common_steps.py:233
    And the extracted date should be "2026-07-15"                       # features/steps/common_steps.py:240
    And the extraction should be complete                               # features/steps/common_steps.py:205
    And the expense should be saved to the database                     # features/steps/common_steps.py:256

  @story-2
  Scenario: Extract expense from free-text message via CLI                                     # features/cli_extraction.feature:22
    Given the LLM extraction service is available                                              # features/steps/common_steps.py:23
    And the expense database is empty                                                          # features/steps/common_steps.py:43
    Given the user describes an expense as "lunch 15.50 eur at Mario's Pizzeria on 2026-07-10" # features/steps/cli_steps.py:117
    When I run the CLI command "extract-from-text" with that text                              # features/steps/cli_steps.py:123
    Then the extracted amount should be "15.50"                                                # features/steps/common_steps.py:219
    And the extracted currency should be "EUR"                                                 # features/steps/common_steps.py:226
    And the extracted merchant should be "Mario's Pizzeria"                                    # features/steps/common_steps.py:233
    And the extracted date should be "2026-07-10"                                              # features/steps/common_steps.py:240
    And the extraction should be complete                                                      # features/steps/common_steps.py:205
    And the expense should be saved to the database                                            # features/steps/common_steps.py:256

  @story-2
  Scenario: Extract expense with optional category from text                                                              # features/cli_extraction.feature:33
    Given the LLM extraction service is available                                                                         # features/steps/common_steps.py:23
    And the expense database is empty                                                                                     # features/steps/common_steps.py:43
    Given the user describes an expense as "taxi 25 usd transport"                                                        # features/steps/cli_steps.py:117
    And the LLM will extract amount "25.00", currency "USD", merchant "Taxi", date "2026-07-15", and category "transport" # features/steps/cli_steps.py:218
    When I run the CLI command "extract-from-text" with that text                                                         # features/steps/cli_steps.py:123
    Then the extracted amount should be "25.00"                                                                           # features/steps/common_steps.py:219
    And the extracted currency should be "USD"                                                                            # features/steps/common_steps.py:226
    And the extracted category should be "transport"                                                                      # features/steps/common_steps.py:249
    And the expense should be saved to the database                                                                       # features/steps/common_steps.py:256

  Scenario: Partial extraction from ambiguous text                # features/cli_extraction.feature:42
    Given the LLM extraction service is available                 # features/steps/common_steps.py:23
    And the expense database is empty                             # features/steps/common_steps.py:43
    Given the user describes an expense as "something expensive"  # features/steps/cli_steps.py:117
    And the LLM will only extract the amount "100.00"             # features/steps/cli_steps.py:236
    When I run the CLI command "extract-from-text" with that text # features/steps/cli_steps.py:123
    Then the extraction should not be complete                    # features/steps/common_steps.py:212
    And the database should still be empty                        # features/steps/common_steps.py:262

Feature: Correction Loop # features/correction.feature:1
  As a user
  I want to correct partial or wrong extractions
  So that my final stored expenses are accurate
  Feature: Correction Loop  # features/correction.feature:1

  @story-6
  Scenario: Partial extraction from photo prompts for missing fields                 # features/correction.feature:12
    Given the bot is running                                                         # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the extraction service is working                                            # features/steps/common_steps.py:31
    And the database is empty                                                        # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given I have a valid receipt photo                                               # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:20
    When I send a receipt photo                                                      # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:41
    And the LLM extracts only the amount "15.00" without currency, merchant, or date # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:118
    Then the bot should not save any expense                                         # features/steps/common_steps.py:286
    And the bot should ask for missing fields                                        # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:297
    And the missing fields should include "currency", "merchant", and "date"         # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:305
    And the pending correction should be stored for my user                          # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:312

  @story-7 @story-8
  Scenario: User corrects missing fields via text                                                           # features/correction.feature:22
    Given the bot is running                                                                                # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the extraction service is working                                                                   # features/steps/common_steps.py:31
    And the database is empty                                                                               # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given I have a pending correction with amount "15.00" but missing currency, merchant, and date          # features/steps/correction_steps.py:22
    When I reply with the correction text "it was EUR 15 at Ristorante Roma on 2026-07-18"                  # features/steps/correction_steps.py:112
    And the LLM refines the extraction to be complete with merchant "Ristorante Roma" and date "2026-07-18" # features/steps/correction_steps.py:118
    Then the bot should save the expense with all fields                                                    # features/steps/correction_steps.py:250
    And the bot should reply with a confirmation containing "Updated and saved"                             # features/steps/common_steps.py:292
    And the bot should reply with a confirmation containing "Expense #1"                                    # features/steps/common_steps.py:292
    And the bot shows exactly these buttons: "🗑️ Delete"                                                    # features/steps/list_steps.py:198
    And the pending correction should be cleared                                                            # features/steps/correction_steps.py:261

  @story-7 @story-8
  Scenario: User corrects wrong fields from the original extraction                                     # features/correction.feature:33
    Given the bot is running                                                                            # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the extraction service is working                                                               # features/steps/common_steps.py:31
    And the database is empty                                                                           # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given I have a pending correction with amount "20.00", currency "USD", but wrong merchant "Unknown" # features/steps/correction_steps.py:44
    When I reply with the correction text "the merchant was actually Best Western Hotel"                # features/steps/correction_steps.py:112
    And the LLM refines the extraction with merchant "Best Western Hotel"                               # features/steps/correction_steps.py:134
    Then the bot should save the expense with merchant "Best Western Hotel"                             # features/steps/correction_steps.py:267
    And the saved expense should have amount "20.00" and currency "USD"                                 # features/steps/common_steps.py:298
    And the bot should reply with a confirmation containing "Expense #1"                                # features/steps/common_steps.py:292
    And the bot shows exactly these buttons: "🗑️ Delete"                                                # features/steps/list_steps.py:198

  Scenario: Correction still incomplete — ask again                 # features/correction.feature:42
    Given the bot is running                                        # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the extraction service is working                           # features/steps/common_steps.py:31
    And the database is empty                                       # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given I have a pending correction with only amount "10.00"      # features/steps/correction_steps.py:69
    When I reply with the correction text "it was at a cafe"        # features/steps/correction_steps.py:112
    And the LLM refines but still cannot determine currency or date # features/steps/correction_steps.py:147
    Then the bot should not save any expense                        # features/steps/common_steps.py:286
    And the bot should tell me which fields are still missing       # features/steps/correction_steps.py:274
    And the correction attempt count should increase to 2           # features/steps/correction_steps.py:283

  Scenario: Max correction attempts exhausted                                 # features/correction.feature:50
    Given the bot is running                                                  # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the extraction service is working                                     # features/steps/common_steps.py:31
    And the database is empty                                                 # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given I have a pending correction that has already been attempted 3 times # features/steps/correction_steps.py:89
    When I reply with another correction text                                 # features/steps/correction_steps.py:213
    Then the bot should not call the LLM again                                # features/steps/correction_steps.py:292
    And the bot should tell me the extraction could not be completed          # features/steps/correction_steps.py:302
    And the pending correction should be removed                              # features/steps/correction_steps.py:310

Feature: Delete Saved Expenses # features/delete.feature:1
  As a user
  I want to delete saved expenses by id or from the creation message
  So that I can remove mistakes from my records
  Feature: Delete Saved Expenses  # features/delete.feature:1

  @story-17
  Scenario: /delete removes a saved expense and confirms what was deleted                         # features/delete.feature:11
    Given the bot is running                                                                      # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the database is empty                                                                     # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given the following expenses exist:                                                           # features/steps/list_steps.py:15
      | id | amount | currency | merchant    | date       | category  |
      | 1  | 42.50  | EUR      | Supermarket | 2026-07-10 | groceries |
      | 2  | 12.50  | EUR      | Coffee Shop | 2026-07-15 | food      |
    When I send the command "/delete 2"                                                           # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:241
    Then the delete reply should be "🗑️ Deleted expense #2: Coffee Shop — 12.50 EUR — 2026-07-15" # features/steps/delete_steps.py:110
    And expense #2 should no longer be recorded                                                   # features/steps/delete_steps.py:117

  @story-17
  Scenario: /delete reports not found for an expense outside my records  # features/delete.feature:21
    Given the bot is running                                             # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the database is empty                                            # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given the following expenses exist:                                  # features/steps/list_steps.py:15
      | id | amount | currency | merchant      | date       | user_id |
      | 1  | 50.00  | EUR      | User 123 Shop | 2026-07-10 | 123     |
      | 2  | 25.00  | EUR      | User 456 Shop | 2026-07-11 | 456     |
    When user 123 sends the delete command "/delete 2"                   # features/steps/delete_steps.py:14
    Then the delete reply should be "Expense #2 was not found."          # features/steps/delete_steps.py:110
    And expense #2 should still be recorded for user 456                 # features/steps/delete_steps.py:124

  @story-17
  Scenario: Invalid /delete commands show the usage message                  # features/delete.feature:31
    Given the bot is running                                                 # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the database is empty                                                # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    When I send invalid delete commands:                                     # features/steps/delete_steps.py:26
      | command          |
      | /delete          |
      | /delete abc      |
      | /delete 42 extra |
    Then each delete command should reply with "Usage: /delete <expense_id>" # features/steps/delete_steps.py:132

  @story-18
  Scenario: Delete button strikes through the original saved-expense message  # features/delete.feature:40
    Given the bot is running                                                  # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the database is empty                                                 # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given a saved confirmation for expense #1 exists:                         # features/steps/delete_steps.py:84
      | id | amount | currency | merchant     | date       | category |
      | 1  | 3.50   | EUR      | Central Cafe | 2026-07-12 | food     |
    When I tap the delete button for expense #1                               # features/steps/delete_steps.py:44
    Then the edited confirmation still contains "Central Cafe"                # features/steps/delete_steps.py:141
    And the edited confirmation shows struck-through expense details          # features/steps/delete_steps.py:148
    And the edited confirmation includes "🗑️ Deleted."                        # features/steps/delete_steps.py:156
    And the delete button is removed from the edited confirmation             # features/steps/delete_steps.py:163
    And expense #1 should no longer be recorded                               # features/steps/delete_steps.py:117

Feature: Monthly Expense List (Interactive) # features/list.feature:1
  As a user
  I want to browse my expenses by month with inline buttons
  So that I can quickly see what I spent in any month
  Feature: Monthly Expense List (Interactive)  # features/list.feature:1

  @story-11
  Scenario: /list shows current month with total and only months that have expenses  # features/list.feature:11
    Given the bot is running                                                         # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the database is empty                                                        # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given the following expenses exist:                                              # features/steps/list_steps.py:15
      | amount | currency | merchant    | date       | category |
      | 42.50  | EUR      | Supermarket | 2026-07-10 | food     |
      | 12.50  | EUR      | Coffee Shop | 2026-07-20 | food     |
      | 30.00  | EUR      | Book Store  | 2026-03-05 | shopping |
    When I send the command "/list"                                                  # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:241
    Then the message shows expenses for July 2026                                    # features/steps/list_steps.py:143
    And the message lists expense "#1" for merchant "Supermarket"                    # features/steps/list_steps.py:157
    And the message lists expense "#2" for merchant "Coffee Shop"                    # features/steps/list_steps.py:157
    And the message shows the total "55.00"                                          # features/steps/list_steps.py:164
    And the bot shows buttons labeled "2026", "Jul", and "Mar"                       # features/steps/list_steps.py:239
    And the bot does not show a button labeled "2025"                                # features/steps/list_steps.py:192
    And the message explains that only months with expenses are shown                # features/steps/list_steps.py:218

  @story-12
  Scenario: /list with no expenses shows informative message without buttons  # features/list.feature:27
    Given the bot is running                                                  # features/steps/common_steps.py:58
    And the database is empty                                                 # features/steps/common_steps.py:37
    Given I have no expenses recorded                                         # features/steps/common_steps.py:51
    When I send the command "/list"                                           # features/steps/telegram_steps.py:241
    Then the bot replies with a message that no expenses are recorded         # features/steps/list_steps.py:224
    And the bot does not show any year or month buttons                       # features/steps/list_steps.py:232

